1
00:00:03,207 --> 00:00:05,255
Click Edit to open a clip.

2
00:00:05,255 --> 00:00:09,928
Uploading a new file under Audio replaces the old audio everywhere:

3
00:00:09,928 --> 00:00:15,497
the old master copy and every provider's copy are removed once the clip is saved.

4
00:00:16,125 --> 00:00:20,920
A clip marked Provider copy only is lost if you change phone provider,

5
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:23,192
or if the provider deletes it.

6
00:00:23,192 --> 00:00:29,185
To protect it, open the clip, choose the original file again under Audio, and click Save.

7
00:00:29,678 --> 00:00:34,205
Click Re-sync media on a clip to check that every enabled phone provider

8
00:00:34,205 --> 00:00:38,094
still holds it, and to send it to any provider that does not.

9
00:00:38,094 --> 00:00:40,358
Use it after you change provider.

10
00:00:40,814 --> 00:00:43,194
You see a message for each provider:

11
00:00:43,194 --> 00:00:47,102
that it already held the clip, that it received a copy, or that

12
00:00:47,102 --> 00:00:48,689
it did not accept one.

13
00:00:48,689 --> 00:00:51,974
The button appears only on clips with a master copy.

